DESCRIPTION:Guinness World Records Day is the record company's own annual i
 nvitation to break something: a day set aside for attempts staged in schoo
 ls\, offices and town squares\, many of them adjudicated on the spot. Guin
 ness World Records says it was "first held in 2004 to mark Guinness World 
 Records becoming the best-selling copyright book of all time." The date is
  not fixed — the company sets it each year\, and for 2026 its own page g
 ives Thursday\, November 19.\n\nhttps://todaycelebrates.com/holiday/guinne
 ss-world-records-day/
